# Memory Bank Protocol
You are operating in a 64k restricted context window. To prevent memory loss, we use a file-based Memory Bank in the root directory. 

You must maintain these files:
- `memory-bank/product-context.md`: The "why" and core features of the app.
- `memory-bank/system-architecture.md`: The technical stack, file structures, and data models.
- `memory-bank/active-context.md`: What component we are building *right now* and what is blocked.
- `memory-bank/progress.md`: A checklist of what works and what is next.

CRITICAL RULE: Before completing any task or when you feel the context window getting full, you MUST read and update these markdown files to reflect the exact current state of the code.

# CLI Rules
You are working in a Windows 11 environment utilizing powershell. Do not use commands that will return with errors.